WeaveFTPd Changelog
================

1.3.0
-----

Compatibility
- Slave control connections now fail closed. Before upgrading a master/slave
  deployment, configure per-slave mTLS (recommended) or register an IP/CIDR/
  wildcard mask for every slave name. A slave with neither a valid client
  certificate nor a matching mask is refused.
- Sitebot IRC TLS now verifies the server certificate by default. Public IRC
  networks should use `irc.tls_verify: strict`; private CAs should use `custom`
  plus `irc.tls_ca_cert`; `insecure` is available only as an explicit legacy
  fallback.

Security
- Added CA-backed master/slave mTLS. The master requires each client
  certificate Common Name to match the claimed slave name, while slaves can
  verify the master's certificate and hostname through `master_ca_cert`.
- Added persistent per-slave source masks and the `SITE SLAVE MASKS`, `ADDMASK`,
  and `DELMASK` commands for deployments that cannot use mTLS. Global slave
  allow/deny lists remain additional filters rather than authentication.
- Extended auth-state backups to include the persistent slave mask file.

Reliability and race integrity
- Multi-disc races now follow pzs-ng announce naming: `CD1`, `DISC1`, `DISK1`,
  and `DVD1` races retain independent totals but display as
  `Parent.Release/CD1` instead of losing the parent release name.
- Prevented zip races from reporting COMPLETE while the expected part count is
  still unknown. Completion now always requires a known positive total.
- Consolidated SFV checksum-state decisions so an unknown checksum is not
  mistaken for either a verified match or a known mismatch.
- Made published VFS file and directory metadata snapshots immutable, removing
  concurrent reader/writer races during verification, remerge, rename, save,
  and race-stat operations.
- Hardened slave disconnect handling so concurrent response delivery and
  remerge queue shutdown cannot panic, block, or leave stale queue depth.

Audio
- Extended automatic SFV-based `<release>.m3u` generation to FLAC sections.
  `zipscript.audio.create_m3u` now covers both MP3 and FLAC releases and still
  leaves an existing playlist untouched.

Integrations
- Migrated daemon and sitebot IMDb lookups from the retired imdbapi.dev host
  to the schema-compatible api.tiffara.com endpoint.

Setup and documentation
- Added `./setup.sh slavecert <name>` for issuing a separate client identity per
  slave and documented the mTLS and IP-mask upgrade paths.
- Updated the Docker deploy pack to initialize local-slave masks and expose the
  new certificate settings for remote slaves.

1.2.0
-----

Compatibility
- The master-to-slave receive/send commands no longer send speed-policy
  arguments. The current handlers tolerate both the compact and legacy forms,
  but deploy the master and slaves together when rolling this change onto older
  installations.
- Removed daemon-level max-speed throttling entirely. Transfers run uncapped;
  `slowkick` is kick-only and monitors live transfers through plugin services
  instead of passing min/max speed policy into the slave transfer loop.

Performance
- The in-flight path guards no longer build and sort a snapshot of every session.
  Answering "is anyone transferring this one path?" allocated a struct per session
  (plus a RemoteAddr().String() and a deferred recover each) and then sorted the
  whole slice; it now scans the session map directly and stops at the first match.
  These guards run before the 150 on STOR and RETR, so the cost was per raced file.
- The STOR/RETR in-flight conflict guards no longer fan out to every online slave.
  Upload reservations and counted download reservations are established before
  the 150, then combined with the master's session registry. This removes both
  the per-file network fan-out and stale slave snapshots that could briefly report
  a completed transfer as still active.
- Let Linux TCP autotuning manage data-socket buffers by default, with
  `ForceDataSocketBuffers` available for tuned hosts.
- Set TCP_NODELAY on FTP control connections to reduce small-response latency.
- Added TLS session resumption for outbound data connections.
- Race timing now starts at the first real payload file; .sfv/.nfo files no
  longer seed the race window.
- Scoped slave remerges (MarkSubtreeUnseen/PurgeUnseenSubtree) walk the children
  index instead of scanning the full VFS map.
- Per-file -MISSING marker cleanup now runs in the post-upload path instead of
  blocking the upload 226 response.

Reliability
- Fixed `slowkick` aborting a direct-slave transfer without disconnecting the FTP
  control session, which let the same user immediately claim another slot. Local
  and master-proxied data sockets are now tracked and closed during a kick too, so
  disconnecting the session actually interrupts every transfer mode before the
  optional login tempban is applied.
- Fixed browsing getting slower the longer the daemon runs (fast after a restart,
  then seconds to list a small folder). The slave stored a transfer entry for
  every LISTEN/CONNECT data-channel setup but only removed it when a matching
  receive/send actually ran; setups that were aborted, superseded, or never
  connected (very common in FXP racing) leaked forever. That map is range-scanned
  on every CWD into a race directory (for live-transfer stats), so the leak made
  browsing progressively slower until a restart. Transfers are now reaped if a
  receive/send never claims them within a grace window, and aborted-before-start
  setups are dropped immediately.
- Bounded the leech-while-upload "follow" in the slave send path. A download that
  was following a still-running upload of the same file would spin at EOF every
  100ms with no limit; if that upload stalled (but had not finished/aborted) the
  send produced no bytes and the racing client hung until its own timeout, then
  left the file missing -- a retry succeeded because the upload had completed by
  then. The follow now gives up after a bounded idle period so the client fails
  fast and retries cleanly, and each chunk write has a deadline so a receiver that
  stops reading surfaces as an error instead of blocking the send.
- Uploads now self-abort after an idle period with no new bytes (drftpd-style).
  A stalled source previously held the upload slot open indefinitely (the
  poll-tick read deadline just reset and spun); now the dead upload is released,
  which also frees any leech-while-upload download that was following it and
  stops a stuck transfer from holding the master's completion wait for the full
  2h timeout.

Sitebot
- NEW LEADER is now announced at most once per distinct racer per release, only on
  a real overtake, and never in a single-racer race. Close parallel racing made the
  byte-based leader flip-flop, re-announcing "X takes the lead" on nearly every file.

Data integrity
- Replaced the in-progress `.sfv` fake VFS placeholder with a bridge-level
  pending-upload overlay. FTP listings can still show a just-started `.sfv` so
  cbftp queues it, and download routing can target the owning slave, but SFV
  parsing/completion logic no longer treats that pending file as completed VFS
  truth until the final transfer status lands.
- Fixed SFV checks/COMPLETE missing for releases whose .sfv listed payloads with
  a UTF-8 BOM or path prefix (for example `./disc/file.r00`). The master cached
  those names differently from the zipscript lookup, so one expected file stayed
  invisible even though it was present and checksum-valid.
- Fixed a release that was never SFV-checked or announced complete even though the
  .sfv was present on disk. The 0-byte critical-file reject deleted/blocked a good
  .sfv whenever the master momentarily measured it as 0 bytes, so it was never
  parsed or tracked. A critical 0-byte file is now only rejected if the SLAVE
  confirms it has no real content (for a .sfv: the slave parse yields no entries);
  a real .sfv is kept and parsed. Additionally, any file uploaded into a release
  whose .sfv exists but was never cached now re-parses the .sfv from the slave
  (self-healing), so a missed/raced SFV parse can no longer leave a release
  silently un-checked.
- Fixed a complete-on-disk file (commonly a .zip) listing at a SHORT size (e.g.
  444k instead of 4.8M), which made cbftp race it short. A leech/duplicate
  transfer could grow a weak VFS entry to a partial offset via UpdateFileTransferSize
  while the authoritative completion for that entry never ran (the duplicate STOR
  was rejected as "File exists"), leaving the size stuck. UpdateFileTransferSize
  now refuses to touch an entry that already has a verified completion, and the
  listing size-repair was widened from zero-size only to any unverified entry whose
  VFS size is smaller than the race DB's verified size (restored from the DB).
- Intermittently missing COMPLETE race-end announce. The announce only fired on the
  hook of an SFV-listed file at the instant completeness flipped true; if that flapped
  (a finishing parallel sibling still flagged "uploading"), the announce rode onto a
  trailing non-SFV file (cover/.m3u/.nfo) that the old gate rejected, losing it. The
  gate now fires on any file once the release is verified complete (dedup unchanged,
  totals count only SFV files); a CRC-verified file counts present even if a stale
  live-stat lists it uploading; and a post-hook-queue reap race that could drop the
  task carrying the announce was closed.
- Fixed a remerge purge race that deleted just-uploaded files (incl. the .sfv)
  during a live race. Uploads are added to the VFS, but a concurrent remerge
  marks files unseen at scan start and purges anything still unseen at the end;
  a file that landed after the slave snapshot but before the purge was wrongly
  removed. The final purge now spares files modified within the recency grace
  window (matching the per-directory prune), and completed uploads are recorded
  as seen. cbftp reports the race done, so the missing file was never re-sent.
- Fixed the VFS recording a 0/short size for a file that is complete on disk. A
  remerge/re-scan reads the live on-disk size and AddFile would overwrite the
  correct completed size with it (short/0 if it caught a file mid-write); the
  size-preservation guard was scoped to .zip payloads only, so .sfv/.rar/.mp3
  etc. were clobbered. AddFile now refuses to let an evidence-free re-scan (no
  checksum/xfertime) shrink a completed size, for all file types. This was making
  a valid .sfv list as 0 bytes, which cbftp skips, so it never raced.
- weaveftpd now generates the <release>.m3u from the SFV when an MP3 release
  completes, matching glftpd/pzs-ng. It lists the SFV's MP3 files, is written to
  the release's slave before the complete announce/hook fires, and is skipped if
  the release already ships an .m3u. Toggle with audio.create_m3u (default true).
  Without this the m3u only existed if a racer uploaded one, so outbound races
  and link scripts could complete before it arrived.
- passwd, etc/group, and per-group files are now written atomically (temp file
  + rename); group saves are mutex-guarded.
- Fixed truncated .zip volumes counting toward "complete" on master/slave. A zip
  that fails the integrity test by being unopenable (truncated) was reported by
  the slave as an error, which the master treated as "check skipped" and kept the
  file; it is now reported as a failed check and deleted, like a CRC-bad zip and
  like the local path already did. Combined with the leech-while-upload fix this
  stops a zip release from ever reading complete with a short/corrupt volume.
- Fixed cbftp missing one file when racing from one WeaveFTPd into another while
  the source file was still landing. CRC/zip validation deletes now return `426`
  instead of `226`, so clients retry instead of marking a deleted upload as
  successful. In-flight upload collisions now return temporary `450` replies;
  `553 X-DUPE` is reserved for real completed duplicates.
- Fixed stuck "incomplete" releases when two racers/cbftp instances hit the same
  release: a file whose checksum already matches the SFV now counts as present
  even while a concurrent duplicate upload still shows it as "uploading", so a
  finished release no longer flaps to incomplete or leaves a stale -MISSING
  marker.
- REQUEST/REQFILL metadata is now flushed to disk immediately and mirrored to a
  readable JSON state file so REQTOP fill counters survive daemon restarts
  instead of depending on the periodic VFS save loop.
- Fixed intermittent missing .sfv (and .nfo/.diz) on weaveftpd->weaveftpd FXP races.
  Root cause: when a file was FXP-pulled at the same instant a racer was
  uploading it to the source, the "leech-while-upload" detection was only checked
  once at the start of the send, so an upload that registered a moment later was
  missed and the source shipped a 0-byte copy. The send now re-checks at EOF and
  streams the file as it lands (no added delay for finished files). A 0-byte
  .sfv/.nfo/.diz on the destination is also rejected (so the racer re-uploads)
  rather than silently kept, as a safety net.
- Consolidated all auth-state backups into one `backup/` folder of timestamped
  snapshots (pruned to the recent window), replacing the backups that were
  scattered as `etc/passwd-`, `etc/users-/`, per-write `.backup` copies, etc.
  Atomic writes already prevent torn files, so the per-write copies were dropped.

NUKE / UNNUKE
- UNNUKE restores the credits removed at nuke time via the new `nukees_data`
  history column.
- Legacy nuke records restore with the recorded multiplier, defaulting to x1
  when unknown.
- Lifetime nuke stats are decremented for the restored nuke instead of reset.
- Nuke/unnuke rename and credit handling now avoid stranded penalties or double
  restores on rename failure.
- Fixed local-mode absolute-target path handling and unchecked stat casts.

SITE command fixes
- CHMOD validates the mode and reports filesystem errors.
- SITE USER now requires siteop to view other accounts.
- GRPDEL rewrites etc/group so deleted groups no longer reappear on restart.
- SELFIP is available to authenticated non-siteop users again.
- GADMIN can revoke admin and validates group existence/membership; CHGRP and
  CHPGRP reject nonexistent groups.

Other fixes
- User loading honors a non-default `passwd_file` for UID/GID lookup.
- Credit accrual is overflow-safe.
- Removed the always-0 [Speed] field from SITE STAT.

Display
- MP3, FLAC, IMDB and TVMaze info on CWD are now CP437 boxes at one shared width
  matching the race-stats banner.
- The CWD race-stats banner now uses a compact "R A C E S T A T S" title.
- The WeaveFTPd ASCII art moved to the login MOTD.

Plugins
- releaseguard: a banned release can no longer slip in via STOR. An upload that
  auto-creates the release dir now runs the same releaseguard check as an
  explicit MKD, so a 550-on-MKD can't be bypassed by uploading into the dir.
- spacekeeper: refuse min-age rules when a release has no mod time, re-check
  live slave free space during reclaim, bound concurrent archive moves, and log
  rejected rule configs.
- bnc: added per-target `display_host` so a status check can connect over
  loopback while still announcing the public address.

1.1.0b
------

- Expanded built-in SITE command coverage and user management:
  - added `SITE CHANGE`
  - added `SITE CHNUMLOGINS`, `CHMAXSIM`, `CHWKLYALLOTMENT`,
    `CHUPLOADSLOTS`, `CHDOWNLOADSLOTS`, `GROUPSLOTS`, `GROUPSIMULT`,
    `BAN`, `UNBAN`, `BLOWFISH`, `TAGLINE`, and `NUKES`
  - added `SITE ALLUP`, `ALLDN`, `WKUP`, `WKDN`, `DAYUP`, `DAYDN`,
    `MONTHUP`, and `MONTHDN`
  - tightened built-in siteop/gadmin command boundaries so group admins are
    limited to adding users for their own managed groups
- Added persistent nuke history in `userdata/nukes.db` and wired both manual
  and automatic nukes through the same history path, including stored reason,
  multiplier, affected users, bytes, credits, and unnuke tracking.
- Added persistent weekly allotment state in `userdata/weekly_allotment.db`
  so weekly credit replacement survives restarts and only reapplies once per
  week.
- Added banlist-backed login bans in `etc/banlist.txt`.
- Clarified `SITE CHANGE` usage around canonical field names and removed the
  extra compatibility aliases from that command.
- Expanded the shipped userfile model and defaults:
  - fuller compatibility fields such as `LOGINS`, `LOGINSLOTS`, `MAXSIM`,
    `UPLOADSLOTS`, `DOWNLOADSLOTS`, `WKLYALLOTMENT`, `GROUPSLOTS`, and
    `PRIMARY_GROUP`
  - corrected runtime enforcement for login slots, max simultaneous
    transfers, upload/download slots, weekly allotment, and grouped admin
    allowances
  - allowed managed-group leech assignment only through the narrow leech-slot
    path while keeping full ratio changes siteop-only
- Refreshed README and wiki content for the newer slave-mode, remerge, and
  transfer behavior.

1.0.9b
------

- Preserved more VFS directory metadata across restarts and reused cached VFS
  state on the first slave reconnect after master startup instead of forcing a
  pointless initial full remerge.
- Fixed race-complete and race-stats announce edge cases caused by stale
  live-transfer state and over-aggressive complete dedupe.
- Fixed race-complete timing around the last uploaded file so `COMPLETE` and
  follow-up stats lines no longer disappear on successful finishes.
- Reduced race polling pressure on slaves by keeping fresh transfer-state
  reads limited to the completion-critical paths.

1.0.8b
------

- Reduced routine console noise:
  - quieter master/slave non-debug logging
  - hidden routine slave command spam unless debug logging is enabled
  - trimmed successful transfer checksum chatter while keeping mismatch
    warnings
- Tightened slave-mode config handling so slave roots are explicit and
  role-specific config expectations are clearer.
- Refined sitebot output and themes:
  - bandwidth plugin uses the configured site name instead of a hardcoded
    daemon name
  - failed-login staff notices include ready-to-copy ban hints for rejected
    IPs
  - race stats labels/colors were cleaned up, including `ALLUP` naming and
    more consistent rank, speed, and header styling

1.0.7b
------

- Reworked the active/passive transfer path for better secure FXP and
  passthrough stability, including cleaner SSCN/CPSV state handling,
  corrected active TLS role behavior, deferred slave connect timing, and
  tighter transfer-state handoff between master and slave.
- Improved live race transfer behavior, including better secure active upload
  handling, cleaner duplicate-file responses, and more consistent complete
  banner timing under load.
- Added handling for zip-integrity slave responses and improved rescan /
  remerge reporting during large recovery runs.

1.0.6b
------

- Added short post-kick tempbans to `slowkick` so slow users cannot
  reconnect immediately and reclaim the same race slot.
- Extended `slowkick` to watch slow downloads too, with separate
  upload/download thresholds and staff-channel announce events.
- Added the first `spacekeeper` daemon plugin as a master-side free-space
  cleaner that deletes the oldest eligible releases from configured virtual
  paths when a slave drops below its configured free-space threshold.
- Extended `spacekeeper` with archive relocation rules, optional
  dated-folder protection so date buckets are not selected as
  cleanup/archive targets, and background archive jobs including real
  cross-slave archive moves when the archive path routes to another slave.
- Tightened `spacekeeper` archive rules so archive moves are also gated by
  low free space on the watched source slave instead of running every cycle.
- Hardened ACL reloads so malformed `permissions.yml` YAML fails cleanly
  instead of silently degrading into a broken live permissions view.
- Added a `pretime` daemon plugin that can look up release pre times from
  SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL, or HTTP/JSON sources and append `NEWPRETIME` /
  `OLDPRETIME` announces for new release dirs.
- Added a sitebot-side `quota` plugin for trial/quota tracking, staff
  `!quotactl` management, and disabled-user enforcement tied to flag `6`.
- Fixed `SITE RESCAN` for music sorting so refreshed audio metadata also
  rebuilds the genre/artist/year/group sort-tree links.
- Made music sort buckets section-aware by default so MP3 and FLAC no longer
  land in the same genre/year/artist/group trees unless explicitly configured.

1.0.5b
------

- Reworked the in-memory VFS so directory listings use direct child indexes
  instead of broad global scans.
- Added cached race-state reads and RaceDB-backed release search to reduce
  hot-path overhead during browsing and racing.
- Switched the shipped ACL examples to root-based paths (`/PRE`, `/MP3`, etc.)
  and cleaned up the structured permissions examples.
- Moved PRE affil visibility management fully into the PRE plugin so
  `affils.yml` stays the source of truth and generated ACL rules stay in sync.
- Added slave-control hardening:
  - IP allowlist support
  - auth-failure temp bans
  - persistent denylist file
  - `SITE SLAVEBANS`, `SITE SLAVEBAN`, and `SITE SLAVEUNBAN`
- Added the built-in `slowkick` plugin to warn and kick slow uploaders and
  downloaders, with staff-channel announcements.
- Added DH1080 auto-exchange for encrypted PM/NOTICE traffic in the sitebot.
- Fixed a race where very fast slave acknowledgements could arrive before the
  master had registered its waiter, causing random upload timeout failures.
- Fixed zip zipscript handling for `0DAY` and `EBOOKS`:
  - blocks manual `file_id.diz` uploads
  - extracts `file_id.diz` from uploaded archives
  - parses more real-world DIZ count formats
  - uses the recovered count for progress, halfway, and complete banners
- Fixed missing or inconsistent `NEW` announces by synthesizing `NEW` from the
  first real upload when a clean `MKDIR` announce was missed.
- Fixed dated-dir announce handling for layouts such as
  `/0DAY/2026-04-26/release/`.
- Fixed section resolution for nested roots like `FOREIGN`, `PRE`, and
  `ARCHIVE` so announces route to the correct child section.
- Fixed `SITE RESCAN` for audio releases so cached music metadata such as genre
  and year is refreshed again for complete banners.
- Fixed parent incomplete markers for zip releases.
- Fixed root and section banner leakage so race banners only appear where they
  make sense, and made the normal CWD banner configurable.
- Fixed topic command behavior and PM encryption flow in the sitebot.

1.0.4b
------

- Added the built-in zipscript module with tighter ZIP and SFV handling.
- Added `SITE BW` plus sitebot `!bw`.
- Added `SITE REMERGE`.
- Added request plugin improvements and public request handling.
- Added configurable log mirroring and log retention controls.
- Added music genre to COMPLETE banners.
- Added section directory creation on slaves and better request visibility on
  CWD.
- Fixed nested section routing and release detection for sitebot announces.
- Fixed incomplete markers for dated release dirs and section roots.
- Fixed private-path event suppression and improved normal-user listing
  behavior.

1.0.3b
------

- Introduced the unified `setup.sh` flow and split plugin configs into
  `config.yml.dist` templates.
- Added setup-driven TLS certificate generation and more complete interactive
  config handling.
- Added self-service IP management and autonuke support.
- Added version propagation into startup banners and media banners.
- Added built-in site user and group management improvements.
- Improved logging defaults, disabled debug in shipped examples, and tightened
  rehash output.
- Improved race stat formatting and restored cached SFV state during reconcile.

1.0.2b
------

- Large architecture refresh of daemon and sitebot internals.
- Added async plugin flow, unified config layout, and broader IRC output
  cleanup.
- Added `SITE PRE`, PREBW support, dated sections, `SITE REHASH`, and
  `SITE INVITE`.
- Added MLST/MLSD support and cbftp-related listing fixes.
- Added metadata lookup groundwork and IMDb rewrite work.
- Improved race speed handling and general announce routing.

1.0.1b
------

- Fixed bcrypt password handling.
- Fixed wrong output from several SITE commands.
- Improved race rendering and race database plumbing.
- Expanded site user management behavior.

1.0.0b
------

- Initial beta baseline for the current WeaveFTPd codebase.
- Core FTP daemon, sitebot, VFS, ACL, and race-tracking foundations in place.
